timestamp=2026-11-04T12:31:17.390Z level=INFO run=6f824f8b message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python -c \"\n# They are only IQR outliers for avg_glucose_level, not for age or bmi. So in our earlier debug2b where we added by other columns - that didn't happen. But then why did debug2b say 'True True True' after step 2 AND also didn't print 'ADDED by...' for age/bmi? That means they were NOT added by age/bmi. They must have been added by avg_glucose_level rule. But the avg_glucose_level branch in our step 2 as written in debug2b adds only if pct < 0.5; otherwise continues without adding. So for these cases, it should continue and NOT add - hence they should NOT be in outlier_set. That contradicts debug2b's final output.\npass\n\" 2>&1" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
